Cost, Qualification, and Technical Challenges

Radiation-hardened SSDs must satisfy demanding reliability requirements, which can increase design, testing, and qualification costs. Specialized components and lower production volumes may also make these products more expensive than conventional commercial storage devices.

Manufacturers must determine how much radiation protection is appropriate for each application. Excessive protection can increase cost and complexity, while insufficient resilience may compromise data integrity and mission reliability.

Long qualification cycles, export restrictions, supply-chain constraints, and the need for long-term component availability can further influence procurement decisions in aerospace and defense markets.

